REQ-ZRM-BASE
When the analysis dictionary contains a configuration block derived from ZermeloTrjGen,
the program shall execute a trajectory-generation workflow
for a specified single start point and a single destination point.
Implementation
ZermeloTrjGen shall:
-own common configuration parsing and validation;
-determine the trajectory space from the common height-range settings;
-read optional startPoint and endPoint from the top level of
  system/fsStreamLineDict as three-component points in the route plane;
  default them to the length-weighted centers of the start and destination
  patch intersections at the corridor midheight;
-read the obstaclePatches, use ground as the default value for obstaclePatches;
-use the common non-negative minObstacleClearance from fsStreamLineDict, defaulting to zero;
-accept zero clearance as disabling obstacle expansion;
-require a positive deviceSpeed when specified, use 0.1 m/s as the default deviceSpeed;
-compute intersections between the trajectory space and the configured obstacle patches;
-prepare obstacle representations expanded by minObstacleClearance;
-invoke a derived-class trajectory-construction strategy to find the shortest
  feasible trajectory between the specified points;
-compute trajectory length from the trajectory geometry returned by the derived strategy;
-compute travel time from trajectory length and deviceSpeed;
-collect the trajectory result;
-if no valid trajectory exists, do not write trajectory output and report this
  condition in the application log;
If variableHeight is enabled and the selected generator does not support variable-height routing,
the program shall terminate with a configuration error.
Related class: ZermeloTrjGen

REQ-ZRM-NOFLOW
When the analysis dictionary contains a ZermeloTrjNoFlow block, the program shall generate a trajectory between the specified single start point and single destination point without using flow-field information. The generated trajectory shall not depend on velocity, pressure, turbulence, or any other flow-field quantity.

Implementation
ZermeloTrjNoFlow shall:
-derive from ZermeloTrjGen;
-generate the trajectory in a horizontal plane located at the midpoint of minHeight and maxHeight;
-use the single start point, single destination point, and obstacle representations prepared by ZermeloTrjGen;
-construct a visibility graph using trajectory endpoints and obstacle geometry;
-determine the shortest collision-free piecewise-linear trajectory between the specified start point and destination point;
-ensure that no trajectory segment enters the interior of an expanded
  obstacle; visibility-graph contact with obstacle boundaries is permitted;
-return the trajectory geometry to the base workflow for result processing;
-report the trajectory as unreachable when no collision-free path exists.
-Variable-height routing is outside the scope of this generator. If variableHeight is enabled, the generator shall terminate with a configuration error.
Related class: ZermeloTrjNoFlow : public ZermeloTrjGen

REQ-NOFLOW-ZRM-trajectory
For the specified single start point and destination point, the program shall generate a collision-free trajectory.
If no feasible trajectory exists, the trajectory shall be reported as unreachable.
Implementation
For the specified start and destination points:
-the generator shall use the fixed-height trajectory plane defined by the base workflow;
-the generator shall use the expanded obstacle footprints prepared by the base workflow;
-the generator shall construct a visibility graph from obstacle vertices and trajectory endpoints;
-the generator shall determine the shortest collision-free piecewise-linear trajectory from the start point to the destination point;
-trajectory segments shall not enter the interior of expanded obstacle
footprints; visibility-graph contact with their boundaries is permitted;
if no collision-free trajectory exists, the generator shall report the trajectory as unreachable and shall not generate trajectory geometry for that path.
The trajectory-generation algorithm shall be purely geometric and shall not depend on any flow-field quantity.
Related class: ZermeloTrjNoFlow

REQ-ZRM-OUTPUT
The program shall write Zermelo trajectory results separately from streamline results for the specified start and end points.
Implementation
The results shall be written to the analysis case's postProcessing directory.
For each generated trajectory, log.fslFoam shall report its startPoint and
endPoint.
File postProcessing/zermelo-no-flow-tracks.vtk shall contain the trajectory
geometry.
File postProcessing/zermelo-no-flow-lines.vtk shall contain the trajectory
geometry and, for every optimal trajectory:
-trajectory identifier;
-trajectory length;
-travel time.
If no feasible trajectory exists, no trajectory files shall remain as output;
the application shall report this condition in its log.

Trajectory output shall be produced through a dedicated Zermelo trajectory
writer.

Related class: ZermeloTrajectoryWriter